{"height":220,"interaction":{"edges":{"e:Lax461425Proofs.Rigidification.exists_reduced:assumption:Lax461425.ReducedRigid:0":{"kind":"assumption","semanticIds":["Lax461425Proofs.Rigidification.exists_reduced:assumption:Lax461425.ReducedRigid"],"source":"c:Lax461425.ReducedRigid","sourceSemanticId":"Lax461425.ReducedRigid","target":"p:Lax461425Proofs.Rigidification.exists_reduced","targetSemanticId":"Lax461425Proofs.Rigidification.exists_reduced"},"e:Lax461425Proofs.Rigidification.exists_reduced:conclusion:Lax461425.Rigidification.exists_reduced:0":{"kind":"conclusion","semanticIds":["Lax461425Proofs.Rigidification.exists_reduced:conclusion:Lax461425.Rigidification.exists_reduced"],"source":"p:Lax461425Proofs.Rigidification.exists_reduced","sourceSemanticId":"Lax461425Proofs.Rigidification.exists_reduced","target":"s:Lax461425.Rigidification.exists_reduced","targetSemanticId":"Lax461425.Rigidification.exists_reduced"}},"nodes":{"c:Lax461425.ReducedRigid":{"href":"../lax-461425/Lax461425.ReducedRigid.html","incident":["e:Lax461425Proofs.Rigidification.exists_reduced:assumption:Lax461425.ReducedRigid:0"],"kind":"concept","label":"Reduced circuits are rigid","nodeId":"c:Lax461425.ReducedRigid","semanticId":"Lax461425.ReducedRigid","tooltipHtml":"Reduced circuits are rigid"},"p:Lax461425Proofs.Rigidification.exists_reduced":{"href":"../lax-461425/Lax461425Proofs.Rigidification.exists_reduced.html","incident":["e:Lax461425Proofs.Rigidification.exists_reduced:assumption:Lax461425.ReducedRigid:0","e:Lax461425Proofs.Rigidification.exists_reduced:conclusion:Lax461425.Rigidification.exists_reduced:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Given a matrix-symmetric circuit `C`, the circuit `C' := RigidConstruction.reduced C` is\nobtained by merging gates that are equivalent under a height-indexed recursive equivalence\nrelation (`RigidEquiv.Equiv`): input gates are equivalent iff they share a label, and internal\ngates of matching height and label are equivalent iff they send the same total wire weight,\naggregated by equivalence class (`RigidWeight.W`), into every class of smaller height. `C'`\nkeeps only the classes (canonical representatives chosen via `RigidRep.rep`) from which the\nclass of the output gate can still be reached. `C'` is reduced because distinct classes are\nnever merged (`RigidReduced.isReduced_reduced`); it computes the same polynomial because every\ngate computes what its class computes (`RigidComputes.computes_transfer`, via a determinism\nlemma for `ComputesAt`); it has size and depth at most those of `C` because classes are\ncollapsed gates/wires (`RigidSize.size_reduced_le`) and every path of `C'` lifts to a\nsame-length path of `C` (`RigidDepth.depth_reduced_le`); it is matrix-symmetric because every\nautomorphism of `C` preserves the equivalence relation and height (`RigidSymmetric`), hence\ninduces an automorphism of `C'` extending the same renaming; and since `C'` is reduced and\nmatrix-symmetric it is rigid (`Lax461425.ReducedRigid.isRigid`), which forces every\nautomorphism of `C'` to be induced this way, so orbits of `C'` are images of orbits of `C` and\nhence no larger (`RigidOrbit.orbitSize_reduced_le`).","nodeId":"p:Lax461425Proofs.Rigidification.exists_reduced","semanticId":"Lax461425Proofs.Rigidification.exists_reduced","tooltipHtml":"Given a matrix-symmetric circuit <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">C</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span></span></span></span>, the circuit <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo mathvariant=\"normal\" lspace=\"0em\" rspace=\"0em\">′</mo